==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*blōþą||blood}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|blōd}}, {{cog|ofs|blōd}}, {{cog|osx|blōd}}, {{cog|odt|bluot}}, {{cog|goh|bluot}}, {{cog|got|𐌱𐌻𐍉𐌸}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|non|/ˈbloːð/|a=12th century Icelandic}}

===Noun===
{{non-noun|n|blóðs}}

# [[blood]]
#* ''{{w|Vǫluspá}}'', verse 9, lines 7-8, in '''1860''', T. Möbius, ''Edda Sæmundar hins fróða: mit einem Anhang zum Theil bisher ungedruckter Gedichte''. Leipzig, page [https://archive.org/stream/eddasmundarhins00mbgoog#page/n23 2]:
#*: {{...}} or brimi '''bloðgu''' / ok or bláin leggju.
#*: {{...}} ''from Brimir's '''blood''' ''/'' and from Blain's limbs.''
# {{lb|non|metaphorically}} [[offspring]]
#* ''{{w|Stjórn}}'' 16, in '''1862''', C. R. Unger, ''Stjórn: gammelnorsk Bibelhistorie: fra Verdens Skabelse til det babyloniske Fangenskab''. Christiania, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=sCtTAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA47 47]:
#*: {{...}} þeir sem hans '''blóð''' ok afkuemi uaru drucknuðu ok fyrirforuz i Noa floði.
#*: {{...}} ''those of his '''offspring''' and progeny drowned and died in Noah's flood.''

